From 6b48bfb52c01cdcf4cc26ffb5bce60e576c2b2cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:58:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 021/110] ARM: sprd: SC7730 secondary CPU bring-up

Cores 1-3 come out of reset into the boot ROM, which waits for their bit
in the AP AHB HOLDING_PEN register and jumps to JMP_ADDR_CA7_Cn, in
Secure SVC mode. Power comes from the PMU: PD_CA7_Cn_CFG without
FORCE_SHUTDOWN powers a core up, PWR_STATUS0_DBG has its state (0 on,
7 off). Sequence from the vendor kernel, confirmed by booting core 1
into a probe stub from user space first. The vendor's software pen is
not needed, the ROM jumps straight to secondary_startup_arm.

Each core sets its own CNTFRQ. Hotplug: the dying core leaves coherency
and waits in WFI, the killer waits for STANDBYWFI before forcing the
power down. AUTO_SHUTDOWN stays off.

Tested on the gtelwifi: four cores at boot, sha256 on four cores in
parallel 3.8x faster than on one with identical results, 50 hotplug
cycles of CPU1 with the core powered off each time, 100 x 10 ms sleeps
in 1.10 s.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/sc7730.dtsi |  21 +++-
 arch/arm/mach-sprd/Makefile          |   1 +
 arch/arm/mach-sprd/platsmp.c         | 141 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 162 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-sprd/platsmp.c

